| Symbol      | One-line Explanation                      |                                        |                                     |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `/`         | Root directory or path separator          |                                        |                                     |
| `~`         | User’s home directory                     |                                        |                                     |
| `.`         | Current directory                         |                                        |                                     |
| `..`        | Parent directory                          |                                        |                                     |
| `*`         | Matches all files/characters              |                                        |                                     |
| `?`         | Matches single character                  |                                        |                                     |
| `>`         | Redirects output to a file                |                                        |                                     |
| `>>`        | Appends output to a file                  |                                        |                                     |
| `<`         | Takes input from a file                   |                                        |                                     |
| `           | `                                         | Sends output of one command to another |                                     |
| `&`         | Runs process in background                |                                        |                                     |
| `&&`        | Runs next command if previous succeeds    |                                        |                                     |
| `           |                                           | `                                      | Runs next command if previous fails |
| `$`         | Accesses variable value                   |                                        |                                     |
| `#`         | Comment or root user prompt               |                                        |                                     |
| `;`         | Executes multiple commands sequentially   |                                        |                                     |
| `' '`       | Treats text literally                     |                                        |                                     |
| `" "`       | Allows variable expansion inside text     |                                        |                                     |
| `+x`        | Adds execute permission                   |                                        |                                     |
| `^`         | Start of line (regex)                     |                                        |                                     |
| `$` (regex) | End of line (regex)                       |                                        |                                     |
| `()`        | Groups commands or expressions            |                                        |                                     |
| `{}`        | Groups multiple commands/variables        |                                        |                                     |
| `[]`        | Used for conditions or character matching |                                        |                                     |
| `\`         | Escape character                          |                                        |                                     |
| `!`         | Negation or command history               |                                        |                                     |
| `sudo`      | Executes command as superuser             |                                        |                                     |
| `grep`      | Searches text patterns                    |                                        |                                     |
| `chmod`     | Changes file permissions                  |                                        |                                     |
| `ps`        | Shows running processes                   |                                        |                                     |
| `kill`      | Terminates a process                      |                                        |                                     |
| `pwd`       | Prints current directory                  |                                        |                                     |
| `ls`        | Lists files/directories                   |                                        |                                     |
| `cd`        | Changes directory                         |                                        |                                     |
| `mkdir`     | Creates directory                         |                                        |                                     |
| `rm`        | Removes files/directories                 |                                        |                                     |
| `cp`        | Copies files/directories                  |                                        |                                     |
| `mv`        | Moves or renames files                    |                                        |                                     |
